{
  "notes": "Sunset synthwave on a worn VHS tape, D major, 92 BPM with a light swing. An FM electric piano (DX RHODES) comps rootless seventh voicings in a syncopated sixteenth figure, a square FUNK BASS slides between roots and octave pops, the player's brassy CZ lead (PHASE CZ BRASS) on the Smart Keys, and the 80S kit (a Linn-style machine) with a big snare. The tape: slow deep chorus wobble, a dark triplet echo and a little hiss. Scenes: A rests on Imaj7 and IVmaj7; B rides IVmaj7 V iii7 vi7; C opens to vi7 IVmaj7 Imaj7 V over four on the floor with open hats; D drifts on vi7 and IVmaj7 in a longer room. ENERGY: the piano alone, then kick and bass, then snare, clap and eighth hats, then swung sixteenth hats, open hats, ratchets and fills. All material is original.",
